## 5.1 Handler chain and Java dependencies

```properties
# ============================================================
# GOLDENGATE JAVA DELIVERY
# ============================================================

gg.handlerlist=filewriter

# Paths produced by the GoldenGate Dependency Downloader.
# Replace these with the installed versions and locations.

gg.classpath=\
/u01/app/ogg/opt/DependencyDownloader/dependencies/s3_<version>/*:\
/u01/app/ogg/opt/DependencyDownloader/dependencies/hadoop_<version>/*:\
/u01/app/ogg/opt/DependencyDownloader/dependencies/parquet_<version>/*
```

Oracle’s S3 Parquet quickstart requires the S3, Hadoop and Parquet client dependencies.

---

## 5.2 File Writer Handler

```properties
# ============================================================
# FILE WRITER HANDLER
# ============================================================

gg.handler.filewriter.type=filewriter
gg.handler.filewriter.mode=op

# Temporary local staging paths.
# These paths must be on durable local storage with enough capacity.

gg.handler.filewriter.pathMappingTemplate=\
./dirout/${fullyQualifiedTableName}

gg.handler.filewriter.stateFileDirectory=./dirsta

gg.handler.filewriter.fileNameMappingTemplate=\
${fullyQualifiedTableName}_${groupName}_\
${currentTimestamp[yyyyMMdd'T'HHmmssSSS]}_${uuid}.avro

gg.handler.filewriter.fileWriteActiveSuffix=.tmp

# Separate writer state by source table.
gg.handler.filewriter.partitionByTable=true

# File rollover.
gg.handler.filewriter.maxFileSize=256m
gg.handler.filewriter.fileRollInterval=10m
gg.handler.filewriter.inactivityRollInterval=2m
gg.handler.filewriter.rollOnShutdown=true

# Delete temporary Avro OCF after downstream handlers succeed.
gg.handler.filewriter.finalizeAction=delete

# The Parquet Handler only accepts Avro OCF internally.
gg.handler.filewriter.format=avro_op_ocf

# Send every completed staging file to the Parquet Handler.
gg.handler.filewriter.eventHandler=parquet
```

Oracle documents the File Writer properties, including maximum size, time-based rollover, inactivity rollover, active-file suffix, state directory and roll-on-shutdown.

Oracle recommends configuring at least two rollover conditions. For Parquet analytics workloads, Oracle identifies 256–512 MB as a common file-size range and 5–15 minutes as a typical near-real-time roll interval.

The Parquet Event Handler only accepts `avro_row_ocf` or `avro_op_ocf` as its temporary upstream format.

The resulting data-lake objects are Parquet; the `.avro` files exist only in GoldenGate’s local staging area.

