## 5.3 Operation-format settings

```properties
# ============================================================
# CDC OPERATION FORMAT
# ============================================================

# Represent a primary-key update as:
# DELETE old key + INSERT new key.

gg.handler.filewriter.format.pkUpdateHandling=delete-insert

# Distinguish a source NULL from a column missing in the trail image.

gg.handler.filewriter.format.includeIsMissingFields=true

# Preserve Oracle DATE/TIMESTAMP as timestamp logical types.

gg.handler.filewriter.format.enableTimestampLogicalType=true
gg.format.timestamp=yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss.SSSSSS

# Preserve numeric/decimal semantics.

gg.handler.filewriter.format.enableDecimalLogicalType=true
```

Oracle recommends `delete-insert` for primary-key updates written to immutable data-lake formats. It requires sufficiently complete source before and after images.

`includeIsMissingFields=true` adds a Boolean field for each source column, allowing consumers to distinguish:

```text
value is SQL NULL
```

from:

```text
column was absent from the trail image
```

Oracle DATE and TIMESTAMP values are otherwise written as strings by default. `enableTimestampLogicalType=true` maps them through the Avro `timestamp-micros` logical type used to generate the final Parquet schema.

For Oracle `NUMBER` columns without declared precision and scale, do not set a global `maxPrecision` or `oracleNumberScale` until the source columns have been profiled. Oracle warns that an incorrectly restrictive maximum precision can cause Replicat to ABEND at runtime.

