## 5.4 GoldenGate metadata fields

```properties
# ============================================================
# DATA PLATFORM TECHNICAL FIELDS
# ============================================================

gg.handler.filewriter.format.metaColumnsTemplate=\
${static[dptf_source_system].oracle_trade},\
${static[dptf_source_database].trading_prod},\
${schema[dptf_source_schema]},\
${table[dptf_source_table]},\
${objectname[dptf_source_object]},\
${optype[dptf_operation_type]},\
${timestamp[dptf_source_operation_ts]},\
${timestampmicro[dptf_source_operation_ts_epoch_us]},\
${currenttimestampiso8601[dptf_ingestion_ts]},\
${currenttimestampmicro[dptf_ingestion_ts_epoch_us]},\
${csn[dptf_source_csn]},\
${xid[dptf_source_transaction_id]},\
${opseqno[dptf_transaction_operation_seq]},\
${txind[dptf_transaction_indicator]},\
${position[dptf_trail_position]},\
${seqno[dptf_trail_sequence]},\
${rba[dptf_trail_rba]},\
${primarykeycolumns[dptf_primary_key_columns]},\
${primarykeysmap[dptf_primary_keys]},\
${metadatachanged[dptf_schema_changed]},\
${groupname[dptf_replicat_group]}
```

GoldenGate no longer emits metadata columns automatically; they must be explicitly configured using `format.metaColumnsTemplate`. The output name can be supplied in brackets, which permits the `dptf_` naming convention.

### Metadata reference

| GoldenGate keyword           | Output field                        | Meaning                                              |
| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `${schema}`                  | `dptf_source_schema`                | Source schema                                        |
| `${table}`                   | `dptf_source_table`                 | Source table                                         |
| `${objectname}`              | `dptf_source_object`                | Fully qualified source object                        |
| `${optype}`                  | `dptf_operation_type`               | Insert, update, delete or truncate                   |
| `${timestamp}`               | `dptf_source_operation_ts`          | Stable source trail operation timestamp              |
| `${timestampmicro}`          | `dptf_source_operation_ts_epoch_us` | Source timestamp as epoch microseconds               |
| `${currenttimestampiso8601}` | `dptf_ingestion_ts`                 | Time GoldenGate formatted the record                 |
| `${csn}`                     | `dptf_source_csn`                   | Source commit sequence number                        |
| `${xid}`                     | `dptf_source_transaction_id`        | Source transaction identifier                        |
| `${opseqno}`                 | `dptf_transaction_operation_seq`    | Record sequence within the transaction               |
| `${txind}`                   | `dptf_transaction_indicator`        | Beginning, middle, end or whole transaction          |
| `${position}`                | `dptf_trail_position`               | Concatenated trail sequence and RBA                  |
| `${seqno}`                   | `dptf_trail_sequence`               | Trail file sequence                                  |
| `${rba}`                     | `dptf_trail_rba`                    | Record offset in the trail                           |
| `${primarykeycolumns}`       | `dptf_primary_key_columns`          | List of primary-key column names                     |
| `${primarykeysmap}`          | `dptf_primary_keys`                 | Map of primary-key names and values                  |
| `${metadatachanged}`         | `dptf_schema_changed`               | True for the first operation after a metadata change |
| `${groupname}`               | `dptf_replicat_group`               | Replicat process name                                |

Oracle’s complete metacolumn keyword reference defines `position`, `csn`, `xid`, `opseqno`, `txind`, primary-key metadata, `metadatachanged` and `groupname`.

The source operation timestamp is stable when the trail is replayed. The current/ingestion timestamp is generated when the formatter processes the event and can change during replay.

Therefore, use:

```text
dptf_source_operation_ts
dptf_source_csn
dptf_trail_position
```

for source ordering and identity.

Do not use:

```text
dptf_ingestion_ts
```

as part of the deterministic event identifier.

