## 5.5 Hourly partition configuration

The partition configuration belongs to the File Writer Handler:

```properties
# ============================================================
# HOURLY INGESTION PARTITIONS
# ============================================================

gg.handler.filewriter.partitioner.TRADE.EXECUTIONS=\
dptf_ingest_date=${currentTimestamp[yyyy-MM-dd]}/\
dptf_ingest_hour=${currentTimestamp[HH]}

gg.handler.filewriter.partitioner.TRADE.ORDERS=\
dptf_ingest_date=${currentTimestamp[yyyy-MM-dd]}/\
dptf_ingest_hour=${currentTimestamp[HH]}

gg.handler.filewriter.partitioner.TRADE.TRADES=\
dptf_ingest_date=${currentTimestamp[yyyy-MM-dd]}/\
dptf_ingest_hour=${currentTimestamp[HH]}

gg.handler.filewriter.partitioner.TRADE.FILLS=\
dptf_ingest_date=${currentTimestamp[yyyy-MM-dd]}/\
dptf_ingest_hour=${currentTimestamp[HH]}

# Generate one partitioner property for every captured table.
```

Oracle’s documented syntax is:

```properties
gg.handler.filewriter.partitioner.<fully-qualified-table-name>=<partition-template>
```

Data must first be separated by table using `partitionByTable=true`. The resolved partition path is passed to the downstream Parquet and S3 handlers.

GoldenGate’s `currentTimestamp` is used here intentionally because these are **ingestion partitions**.

The partition values are not the authoritative Oracle commit time. That remains available as:

```text
dptf_source_operation_ts
```

