## 5.6 Parquet Event Handler

```properties
# ============================================================
# PARQUET EVENT HANDLER
# ============================================================

gg.eventhandler.parquet.type=parquet
gg.eventhandler.parquet.writeToHDFS=false

gg.eventhandler.parquet.pathMappingTemplate=./dirparquet

gg.eventhandler.parquet.fileNameMappingTemplate=\
${fullyQualifiedTableName}_${groupName}_\
${currentTimestamp[yyyyMMdd'T'HHmmssSSS]}_${uuid}.parquet

gg.eventhandler.parquet.compressionCodec=SNAPPY
gg.eventhandler.parquet.dictionaryEncoding=true

# Delete the local Parquet file after successful S3 upload.
gg.eventhandler.parquet.finalizeAction=delete

# Send the completed Parquet file to the S3 Handler.
gg.eventhandler.parquet.eventHandler=s3
```

Oracle supports `GZIP`, `LZO`, `SNAPPY` and `UNCOMPRESSED` Parquet compression. It also exposes dictionary encoding, row-group sizing and validation settings.

Leave Parquet row-group and page-size settings at the library defaults initially. Tune them only after observing representative file sizes and Spark scan performance.

